  "task": "Evaluate whether the pull request commit-count and per-commit file-count push gates earn their cost, and structurally solve what the evidence shows. Produced ADR-100 (retire the size ceilings) and ADR-101 (enforcement planes), carried through eleven rounds of six-role adr-review plus continuing external bot review. The round count is stated rather than a finding count, because a count of findings here goes stale on every subsequent round and this field is copied verbatim into the episode artifact. Consensus was reached twice: at round 6, on text later shown to hold more than a dozen factual errors, and at round 11 on the revision under review at that time. **Not on the current text**, and an earlier revision of this field said so, which was false by the time it was written and matters more here than elsewhere because extract_session_episode.py copies this field verbatim into the episode that feeds memory retrieval. Material ADR changes landed after round 11 and the panel has not seen them, because the ten-round cap forecloses a round 12. The difference between them is that rounds 8 through 11 assigned verification against the tree, after which every substantive finding came from running or reading a primary source rather than from re-reading prose.",
